WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.156 --> 00:00:05.756
♪ ♪

00:00:05.757 --> 00:00:07.357
&gt;&gt; Tucker: WELL, THE PERCENTAGE

00:00:07.358 --> 00:00:08.992
OF FOREIGNS BORN IN THE UNITED

00:00:08.993 --> 00:00:11.795
STATES IS THE HIGHEST IT'S BEEN

00:00:11.796 --> 00:00:12.563
IN THE CENTURY.

00:00:12.564 --> 00:00:16.233
IT'S STILL RISING IN ANY CASE.

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:18.135
67 MILLION AMERICANS SPEAK A

00:00:18.136 --> 00:00:20.604
LANGUAGE OTHER THAN ENGLISH AT

00:00:20.605 --> 00:00:20.904
HOME.

00:00:20.905 --> 00:00:21.638
PRETTY MUCH EVERYONE IN

00:00:21.639 --> 00:00:23.307
WASHINGTON IS FINE WITH THAT.

00:00:23.308 --> 00:00:24.875
THE NUMBER RISING.

00:00:24.876 --> 00:00:27.878
BUT WHAT WOULD THE EFFECT BE IF

00:00:27.879 --> 00:00:29.146
WE DID THAT?

00:00:29.147 --> 00:00:29.847
WHO IS COMING HERE?

00:00:29.848 --> 00:00:31.482
WHAT ARE THEY LIKE?

00:00:31.483 --> 00:00:38.021
AND WHERE IS ALL OF THIS GOING?

00:00:38.022 --> 00:00:40.023
STEVEN, JUST THE FIRST OBVIOUS

00:00:40.024 --> 00:00:40.424
OBSERVATION.

00:00:40.425 --> 00:00:41.959
PEOPLE WHEN I WAS A KID USED TO

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.428
CARE ABOUT OVERPOPULATION.

00:00:44.429 --> 00:00:46.763
I GUESS NOBODY DOES ANYONE.

00:00:46.764 --> 00:00:48.999
&gt;&gt; THAT'S A FAIR QUESTION.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.636
IMMIGRATION BY 2060 WILL ADD 75

00:00:52.637 --> 00:00:54.671
MILLION PEOPLE TO THE U.S.

00:00:54.672 --> 00:00:55.506
POPULATION.

00:00:55.507 --> 00:00:56.273
YOU WOULD THINK PEOPLE CONCERNED

00:00:56.274 --> 00:00:57.941
ABOUT THE ENVIRONMENT, TRAFFIC,

00:00:57.942 --> 00:00:58.842
POLLUTION WOULD THINK ABOUT

00:00:58.843 --> 00:00:59.142
THAT.

00:00:59.143 --> 00:01:00.777
&gt;&gt; Tucker: BUT THOSE ARE REAL

00:01:00.778 --> 00:01:02.412
CONCERNS, WHICH I WILL ADMIT, AS

00:01:02.413 --> 00:01:05.916
A KID, I MOCKED THE LIBERALS FOR

00:01:05.917 --> 00:01:06.550
HAVING.

00:01:06.551 --> 00:01:10.120
BUT AS I GET OVER, I REALIZE I

00:01:10.121 --> 00:01:11.588
DON'T WANT TO LIVE IN A CROWDED

00:01:11.589 --> 00:01:11.955
PLACE.

00:01:11.956 --> 00:01:13.624
DOES ANYONE ON THE LEFT STILL

00:01:13.625 --> 00:01:14.191
SAY THAT?

00:01:14.192 --> 00:01:15.659
&gt;&gt; THERE ARE A FEW PROGRESSIVES

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:16.326
OUT THERE.

00:01:16.327 --> 00:01:18.061
THEY HAVE A LOT OF PROGRESSIVE

00:01:18.062 --> 00:01:19.897
SUPPORT AND THEY TEND TO FOCUS A

00:01:19.898 --> 00:01:21.765
LOT ON POPULATION GROWTH.

00:01:21.766 --> 00:01:23.033
BUT MOST MAINSTREAM PEOPLE ON

00:01:23.034 --> 00:01:28.705
THE LEFT DON'T TOUCH IT WITH A

00:01:28.706 --> 00:01:30.941
10-FOOT POLE BECAUSE LONG-TERM

00:01:30.942 --> 00:01:32.543
IT'S NEW IMMIGRANTS AND THE

00:01:32.544 --> 00:01:33.076
CHILDREN THEY HAVE.

00:01:33.077 --> 00:01:35.212
AND SO THEY DON'T WANT TO TOUCH

00:01:35.213 --> 00:01:37.014
THE ISSUE ANYMORE.

00:01:37.015 --> 00:01:37.981
&gt;&gt; Tucker: WHAT PERCENTAGE OF

00:01:37.982 --> 00:01:39.116
THE POPULATION?

00:01:39.117 --> 00:01:40.918
&gt;&gt; ABOUT 95% OF THE INCREASE IN

00:01:40.919 --> 00:01:42.319
THE U.S. POPULATION WILL COME

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.354
FROM FUTURE IMMIGRANTS AND THE

00:01:44.355 --> 00:01:45.422
CHILDREN AND GRANDCHILDREN

00:01:45.423 --> 00:01:46.256
THEY'LL HAVE.

00:01:46.257 --> 00:01:48.725
&gt;&gt; Tucker: SO THAT'S ALMOST A

00:01:48.726 --> 00:01:50.027
COMPLETE TURNOVER IN POPULATION.

00:01:50.028 --> 00:01:52.796
&gt;&gt; NO, THAT'S POPULATION GROWTH.

00:01:52.797 --> 00:01:56.333
SO MOST OF ALL THE INCREASE IS

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:57.200
COMING FROM IMMIGRATION.

00:01:57.201 --> 00:01:58.702
&gt;&gt; Tucker: SO THE LANGUAGE

00:01:58.703 --> 00:01:59.436
NUMBERS ARE REALLY INTERESTING

00:01:59.437 --> 00:02:00.737
TO ME.

00:02:00.738 --> 00:02:02.739
ONE IN FIVE PEOPLE LIVING IN

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.341
THIS COUNTRY DOES NOT SPEAK

00:02:04.342 --> 00:02:05.776
ENGLISH AT HOME.

00:02:05.777 --> 00:02:07.477
HAS IT EVER BEEN THAT HIGH?

00:02:07.478 --> 00:02:09.680
&gt;&gt; IT'S HARD TO SAY, BUT IT MAY

00:02:09.681 --> 00:02:12.683
HAVE BEEN THAT HIGH AMOUNT PAST.

00:02:12.684 --> 00:02:13.884
WHAT'S EVEN MORE INTERESTING OR

00:02:13.885 --> 00:02:15.619
PERHAPS MORE TROUBLING IS HOW

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:16.320
CONCENTRATED IT IS.

00:02:16.321 --> 00:02:18.855
THERE ARE ALL KINDS OF AREAS

00:02:18.856 --> 00:02:22.626
WHERE 95% OF THE PEOPLE OR 85%

00:02:22.627 --> 00:02:26.663
OF THE PEOPLE AND 95 AND 85% OF

00:02:26.664 --> 00:02:28.298
THE KIDS IN SCHOOL SPEAK A

00:02:28.299 --> 00:02:29.499
FOREIGN LANGUAGE AT HOME.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:32.469
ONE WONDERS HOW ASSIMILATION CAN

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:33.937
WORK WITH THAT LEVEL OF

00:02:33.938 --> 00:02:37.374
IMMIGRATION AND FOREIGN LANGUAGE

00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:37.908
CONCENTRATION?

00:02:37.909 --> 00:02:39.610
&gt;&gt; Tucker: SO WHAT ARE, BROADLY

00:02:39.611 --> 00:02:42.713
SPEAKING, THE EDUCATION LEVELS

00:02:42.714 --> 00:02:45.682
OF IMMIGRANTS COMING HERE?

00:02:45.683 --> 00:02:47.951
&gt;&gt; IT VARIES.

00:02:47.952 --> 00:02:50.921
&gt;&gt; Tucker: OF COURSE IT DOES.

00:02:50.922 --> 00:02:54.157
&gt;&gt; 80% PLUS OF IMMIGRANTS FROM

00:02:54.158 --> 00:02:56.526
INDIA COME WITH A COLLEGE DEGREE

00:02:56.527 --> 00:02:57.094
OR MORE.

00:02:57.095 --> 00:02:58.362
&gt;&gt; Tucker: SO HOW DOES THAT

00:02:58.363 --> 00:03:00.097
BREAK DOWN?

00:03:00.098 --> 00:03:01.698
WHAT PERCENTAGE FOR IMMIGRANTS

00:03:01.699 --> 00:03:03.066
ARE COMING WITH NO EDUCATION

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:04.568
VERSUS THOSE COMING WITH HIGH

00:03:04.569 --> 00:03:05.802
DEGREES OF EDUCATION?

00:03:05.803 --> 00:03:08.238
&gt;&gt; RIGHT NOW SOMEWHAT OVER A

00:03:08.239 --> 00:03:10.273
FOURTH OF ALL IMMIGRANTS HAVE

00:03:10.274 --> 00:03:10.907
LESS THAN A HIGH SCHOOL

00:03:10.908 --> 00:03:12.009
EDUCATION WHEN THEY COME.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:14.177
A LITTLE OVER A FOURTH ALSO HAVE

00:03:14.178 --> 00:03:16.113
NO MORE THAN A HIGH SCHOOL

00:03:16.114 --> 00:03:16.580
EDUCATION.

00:03:16.581 --> 00:03:17.981
SO A HIGH SCHOOL EDUCATION OR

00:03:17.982 --> 00:03:19.883
LESS IS A LITTLE OVER HALF.

00:03:19.884 --> 00:03:22.719
A LITTLE LESS THAN HALF IS SOME

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.622
COLLEGE OR EVEN COLLEGE AND

00:03:25.623 --> 00:03:27.525
MORE.

00:03:27.659 --> 00:03:28.959
&gt;&gt; Tucker: SO THE MAJORITY HAVE

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:30.127
HIGH SCHOOL OR LESS.

00:03:30.128 --> 00:03:31.995
&gt;&gt; AND WE KNOW THE WELFARE USE

00:03:31.996 --> 00:03:34.464
AND POVERTY IS QUITE HIGH.

00:03:34.465 --> 00:03:36.099
&gt;&gt; Tucker: THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.801
WELL, YOU JUST HEARD, AS

00:03:37.802 --> 00:03:39.636
MILLIONS OF PEOPLE, MANY OF THEM

00:03:39.637 --> 00:03:42.539
LOW SKILLED, HALF, CONTINUE TO

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.540
ENTER THIS COUNTRY, AN OBVIOUS

00:03:43.541 --> 00:03:44.908
QUESTION ARISES.

00:03:44.909 --> 00:03:47.210
WHAT DOES THAT MEAN FOR OUR

00:03:47.211 --> 00:03:52.449
ECONOMY, FOR AMERICA'S WORKING

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:59.222
CLASS?

00:03:59.223 --> 00:04:00.657
THANKS FOR COMING ON.

00:04:00.658 --> 00:04:02.826
&gt;&gt; THANK YOU FOR HAVING ME,

00:04:02.827 --> 00:04:03.160
TUCKER.

00:04:03.161 --> 00:04:04.361
&gt;&gt; Tucker: THERE'S A DEBATE OVER

00:04:04.362 --> 00:04:06.296
WHAT AUTOMATION IS GOING TO DO

00:04:06.297 --> 00:04:06.897
LONG TERM.

00:04:06.898 --> 00:04:07.864
EVERYONE AGREES IT WILL

00:04:07.865 --> 00:04:10.200
ELIMINATE A LOT OF JOBS THAT WE

00:04:10.201 --> 00:04:12.135
CURRENTLY THINK OF AS REAL JOBS.

00:04:12.136 --> 00:04:14.137
THEY'LL BE GONE.

00:04:14.138 --> 00:04:15.472
BUT IS THERE ANY SCENARIO IN THE

00:04:15.473 --> 00:04:18.742
FUTURE AS WE PERCEIVE IT NOW

00:04:18.743 --> 00:04:21.244
WHERE YOU WOULD WANT THEM TO

00:04:21.245 --> 00:04:31.021
HAVE A HIGH SCHOOL THE --

00:04:31.022 --> 00:04:33.857
DIPLOMA OR LESS?

00:04:33.858 --> 00:04:35.559
HOW CONCERNED ARE YOU ABOUT

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:35.859
THAT?

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:37.594
&gt;&gt; I THINK IT'S A CONCERN.

00:04:37.595 --> 00:04:38.528
I THINK IT'S ONE AMONG MANY.

00:04:38.529 --> 00:04:40.163
I THINK THERE ARE A LOT OF

00:04:40.164 --> 00:04:41.832
THINGS WE'RE DOING THAT REALLY

00:04:41.833 --> 00:04:44.067
HURT LESS SKILLED WORKERS.

00:04:44.068 --> 00:04:45.602
THE WAY WE APPROACH IMMIGRATION

00:04:45.603 --> 00:04:46.269
AND EDUCATION.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:48.739
WE DON'T CARE ABOUT EDUCATION

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:50.273
FOR LESS-SKILLED WORKERS.

00:04:50.274 --> 00:04:53.410
WE SAY COLLEGE FOR ALL.

00:04:53.411 --> 00:04:55.946
AND IF YOU DON'T COMPLETE

00:04:55.947 --> 00:04:57.581
COLLEGE, YOU FELL OUT SOMEWHERE

00:04:57.582 --> 00:04:59.182
ALONG THE WAY.

00:04:59.183 --> 00:05:02.285
&gt;&gt; Tucker: SO WHY WOULDN'T YOU

00:05:02.286 --> 00:05:04.087
IF, IF YOU WERE THINKING

00:05:04.088 --> 00:05:05.021
THOUGHTFULLY, IF YOU STARTED

00:05:05.022 --> 00:05:05.822
WITH THE PRESUMPTION THAT SOME

00:05:05.823 --> 00:05:07.524
IMMIGRATION IS GOOD, THAT'S

00:05:07.525 --> 00:05:08.592
WHERE I START ANYWAY.

00:05:08.593 --> 00:05:10.761
WHY WOULDN'T YOU BE THOUGHTFUL

00:05:10.762 --> 00:05:12.129
ABOUT LETTING IN MORE PEOPLE WHO

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:14.664
ALREADY HAVE THE EDUCATION THAT

00:05:14.665 --> 00:05:16.867
YOU THINK YOUR ECONOMY REQUIRES?

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:18.802
&gt;&gt; I THINK THAT'S WHAT WE SHOULD

00:05:18.803 --> 00:05:19.069
DO.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:20.403
MOST ECONOMISTS WOULD LOOK AT

00:05:20.404 --> 00:05:22.239
THE ISSUE AND SAY IF YOU WANT TO

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:23.440
BENEFIT WORKERS AT THE BOTTOM

00:05:23.441 --> 00:05:25.542
AND THEIR WAGES, PRETTY MUCH THE

00:05:25.543 --> 00:05:27.544
MODELS SAY HIGH-SKILLED

00:05:27.545 --> 00:05:30.213
IMMIGRATION IS GOOD FOR

00:05:30.214 --> 00:05:31.982
LOW-SKILLED WORKERS.

00:05:31.983 --> 00:05:34.785
MORE LOW-SKILLED WORKERS JUST

00:05:34.786 --> 00:05:36.887
ADDS MORE COMPETITION TO THE

00:05:36.888 --> 00:05:37.220
MARKET.

00:05:37.221 --> 00:05:38.622
&gt;&gt; Tucker: I'VE HAD THIS DEBATE

00:05:38.623 --> 00:05:40.657
OVER A HUNDRED TIMES ON THIS

00:05:40.658 --> 00:05:42.826
SHOW OVER THE LAST COUPLE OF

00:05:42.827 --> 00:05:43.126
YEARS.

00:05:43.127 --> 00:05:45.662
AND THEY SAY, ALL THE STUDIES

00:05:45.663 --> 00:05:47.164
SAY THAT'S NOT TRUE.

00:05:47.165 --> 00:05:50.367
&gt;&gt; I'M NOT AWARE OF A STUDY THAT

00:05:50.368 --> 00:05:50.934
SHOWS THAT.

00:05:50.935 --> 00:05:55.939
THERE ARE A LOT OF STUDIES THAT

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:58.241
SHOW THE MIX OF IMMIGRANTS

00:05:58.242 --> 00:05:59.342
REFLECTS ROUGHLY WHAT'S IN THE

00:05:59.343 --> 00:05:59.743
POPULATION.

00:05:59.744 --> 00:06:00.277
SO THAT'S OKAY.

00:06:00.278 --> 00:06:02.345
BUT THAT'S THE WRONG QUESTION TO

00:06:02.346 --> 00:06:02.612
ASK.

00:06:02.613 --> 00:06:04.281
THE QUESTION TO ASK WOULD WHICH

00:06:04.282 --> 00:06:05.315
WOULD BE BETTER.

00:06:05.316 --> 00:06:07.284
GIVEN TO HAVE HIGH-SKILLED

00:06:07.285 --> 00:06:08.385
IMMIGRATION, IS IT GOOD TO HAVE

00:06:08.386 --> 00:06:10.654
A LOT OF LOW-SKILLED OR LESS?

00:06:10.655 --> 00:06:12.622
AND WHAT YOU WOULD SAY IS THE

00:06:12.623 --> 00:06:14.758
LESS LOW-SKILLED IMMIGRATION YOU

00:06:14.759 --> 00:06:16.126
HAVE, BETTER THINGS WILL BE FOR

00:06:16.127 --> 00:06:20.130
THE LOW-SKILLED WORKERS THAT ARE

00:06:20.131 --> 00:06:20.430
HERE.

00:06:20.431 --> 00:06:22.365
&gt;&gt; Tucker: IF YOU COULD DO ONE

00:06:22.366 --> 00:06:24.401
THING TO HELP PEOPLE WHO ARE

00:06:24.402 --> 00:06:25.402
STRUGGLING TO REAP THE BENEFITS

00:06:25.403 --> 00:06:28.104
OF OUR ECONOMY, WHAT WOULD IT

00:06:28.105 --> 00:06:28.371
BE?

00:06:28.372 --> 00:06:29.706
&gt;&gt; WELL, I THINK CONCEPTUALLY WE

00:06:29.707 --> 00:06:32.676
HAVE TO VALUE WORK AND SAY IT'S

00:06:32.677 --> 00:06:35.579
NOT JUST ABOUT CONSUMPTION AND

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.247
HOW CHEAP STUFF IS.

00:06:37.248 --> 00:06:38.648
WE ACTUALLY HAVE TO REALIZE IS

00:06:38.649 --> 00:06:40.083
THAT PEOPLE HAVING WORK IS

00:06:40.084 --> 00:06:41.651
WHAT'S MOST IMPORTANT TO THEM.

00:06:41.652 --> 00:06:43.854
&gt;&gt; Tucker: WAIT A SECOND.

00:06:43.855 --> 00:06:45.622
PAYING EVERYBODY OFF WITH THREE

00:06:45.623 --> 00:06:47.190
GRAND A MONTH WON'T BE THE

00:06:47.191 --> 00:06:47.524
ANSWER?

00:06:47.525 --> 00:06:48.758
&gt;&gt; NO, IT'S A DISASTER.

00:06:48.759 --> 00:06:49.826
IT'S A GREAT ANSWER FOR THE

00:06:49.827 --> 00:06:51.261
FOLKS DOING WELL.

00:06:51.262 --> 00:06:53.263
THE FUNNY THING IS, THE HIGHER

00:06:53.264 --> 00:06:56.032
UP THE INCOME LADDER YOU GO, THE

00:06:56.033 --> 00:06:57.968
MORE PEOPLE SAY, OH, NOT

00:06:57.969 --> 00:06:59.135
EVERYONE NEEDS A JOB.

00:06:59.136 --> 00:07:01.304
YOU GO DOWN TO THE BOTTOM END OF

00:07:01.305 --> 00:07:03.840
THE LADDER, PEOPLE SAY, WE WANT

00:07:03.841 --> 00:07:06.843
THE JOBS, BECAUSE THEY

00:07:06.844 --> 00:07:08.044
UNDERSTAND HOW CRITICAL WORK IS

00:07:08.045 --> 00:07:09.880
TO THEIR FAMILIES, THOUGH THEIR

00:07:09.881 --> 00:07:10.280
COMMUNITIES.

00:07:10.281 --> 00:07:11.514
AND IF WE DON'T FOCUS ON THAT,

00:07:11.515 --> 00:07:13.850
IF WE JUST SAY, OH, WE'LL GROW

00:07:13.851 --> 00:07:17.587
THE PIE, WHAT THEY SAY, WE'LL

00:07:17.588 --> 00:07:19.389
JUST SEND EVERYONE A PIECE.

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:22.425
YOU DON'T HAVE TO BAKE YOUR OWN

00:07:22.426 --> 00:07:22.692
PIE.

00:07:22.693 --> 00:07:24.261
WE'LL JUST GIVE YOU A SLICE.

00:07:24.262 --> 00:07:26.263
THAT'S NOT A MODEL FOR A GOOD

00:07:26.264 --> 00:07:26.596
SOCIETY.

00:07:26.597 --> 00:07:28.565
&gt;&gt; Tucker: THAT USED TO BE

00:07:28.566 --> 00:07:28.899
OBVIOUS.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:32.636
&gt;&gt; IT DID UNTIL ABOUT THE MIDDLE

00:07:32.637 --> 00:07:33.970
OF THE CENTURY.

00:07:33.971 --> 00:07:35.071
AS LONG AS PEOPLE HAVE MORE

00:07:35.072 --> 00:07:36.106
STUFF EVERY YEAR, WE'LL CALL

00:07:36.107 --> 00:07:40.144
THAT SUCCESS, BUT THAT'S NOT

